    Merge branch 'r/20.x' into r/21.x
    
    Brings the security fixes released with Opencast 20.6 into 21.x.
    
    New on 21.x with this merge:
    
    - GHSA-jrcq-hch7-gvv5: Only trust X-Forwarded-* headers from configured
      proxies (c23be1df19)
    - GHSA-qqqp-5j2v-jvfp: Only list playlists of the current organization
      (05f870bc9e)
    - GHSA-x4wc-h58f-2wm9: HTML-encode the path query parameter in the REST
      docs servlet (65c5474f6d)
    - GHSA-gr3h-hxr8-phqm: Harden the FreeMarker configuration used by
      DocUtil (74001ac87c)
    
    Already on 21.x as branch-specific commits and therefore not applied a
    second time:
    
    - GHSA-87w3-phwh-q8vx: Reject path traversal sequences in media package
      identifiers (eb0b9fa68f on 20.x, f44c809eb8 on 21.x)
    - GHSA-hgqh-jpvg-xx9f: Enforce write permission when deleting an event
      (139dee420d on 20.x, 3a628085e0 on 21.x)
    
    Every file touched by these two fixes is kept exactly as it is on 21.x.
    This covers the reported conflicts as well as
    AbstractFileSystemAssetStore.java and SchedulerServiceImpl.java, where
    git would otherwise have added a second copy of the new helper methods
    without reporting a conflict.
    
    Adjustments needed for 21.x:
    
    - TrustedProxies: IpAddressMatcher lives in
      org.springframework.security.web.util.matcher in Spring Security 5.
    - RestDocsServlet and its test: use StringEscapeUtils from commons-text,
      since 21.x no longer uses the deprecated commons-lang3 class.
    
    Documentation: releasenotes.md and upgrade.md stay as they are on 21.x.
    The 20.6 release notes section and the 19.x to 20.x upgrade steps do not
    belong into the Opencast 21 documents, and the section on media package
    identifier validation is already identical on both branches. The 20.6
    changelog is merged as usual.
    
